evidence: ostrya_cli::cli::cat_path_resolution_matches_the_tool
spec: format-reference.md#cat
note: the literal-component cases -- `.`, `..`, and an empty component naming
 nothing -- a symlink in a non-final position reporting `Not a directory`
 rather than being followed, a relative symlink target resolved against the
 link's own directory, an absolute one resolved against the commit root, and a
 chain 64 links deep followed to its end. Corpus `C0` holds no symlink to a
 directory, none whose target escapes the tree, and no chain, so the cited test
 builds the tree these need. The same test runs the port alone over a link
 naming itself, which reaches the port's 256-link bound and reports `error: Too
 many levels of symbolic links` where the tool dies on a signal.

