family: M10
subcommand: commit
cell: commit/ancestry-branch-name
setup: repo tree
run: commit --repo=$REPO -b main^ $TREE
ref-run: n-a
expect-exit: 1
expect-stdout: empty
expect-stderr: contains "error: Invalid refspec main^"
oracle: exit-status stdout-text stderr-text refs-bytes inventory
outcome: refused-clean
severity: interop
spec: format-reference.md#revision-syntax
note: a branch name ending in `^` is the second shape resolution shadows, read
 as ancestry, so a ref carrying it is reachable by no revision. The port refuses
 it at the ref write in the words it gives that shape at `refs --create`, and
 leaves `refs/` and `objects/` untouched, which `refs-bytes` and `inventory`
 record for the port alone. `ref-run: n-a` states that the tool has no
 comparable invocation: the base `main` names no ref in this setup and the tool
 dies on a signal, a second crash site beside the `refs --create=NEWREF` one
 (`cli-surface.md`, "P2"). `commit/ancestry-branch-name-resolving-base` below
 cites the test that pins the crash and the two bases the tool does report on.

family: M10
subcommand: commit
cell: commit/ancestry-branch-name-empty-base
setup: repo tree
run: commit --repo=$REPO -b ^ $TREE
expect-exit: 1
expect-stdout: empty
expect-stderr: contains "error: Invalid refspec ^"
ref-expect-exit: 1
ref-expect-stdout: empty
ref-expect-stderr: contains "error: Invalid refspec "
oracle: exit-status stdout-text refs-bytes inventory
outcome: refused-both
severity: interop
spec: format-reference.md#revision-syntax
note: the suffix alone, whose base is empty. Both refuse at exit 1 and write
 nothing, and each names what it read: the port the branch as given and the tool
 the empty base it split off, the tool's empty refspec being a name it searches
 its ref store for and this repository holding no ref. The two texts part, so
 `stderr-text` is no oracle and the two `expect-stderr` fields state each side's
 own substring. `inventory` holds here where the 64-character guard leaves it
 out: the tool reads an ancestry name before it commits the tree, so neither
 side published an object (`cli-surface.md`, "P2").

family: M10
subcommand: commit
cell: commit/ancestry-branch-name-resolving-base
setup: repo-with-commit
outcome: refused-both
severity: interop
evidence: ostrya_cli::cli::commit_ancestry_branch_name_matches_the_tool
spec: format-reference.md#revision-syntax
note: the bases the `repo tree` setup cannot bind, which need a repository
 holding a commit and a tree the commit can read, and the consequence the guard
 stands for. The cited test holds the port's one message against each of the
 tool's three outcomes -- the walk's `Commit <checksum> has no parent` over a
 root commit, the agreeing `Invalid refspec main^` over a commit holding a
 parent, and the signal over an absent base -- pins the fault order ahead of the
 guard, states the interior `^` the guard does not cross, and shows that over a
 ref of the refused shape the tool's `refs` prints nothing and its `prune
 --refs-only` deletes the commit that ref holds.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# commit -- parenting: the branch tip a commit inherits, the two forms that ask
# for a root commit, and the ref a commit must name (Phase 17b1 of
# `../port-plan.md`).
#
# A parent is a field of the commit object, so a cell that states one reads the
# new commit with a second invocation. Those cells cite `evidence:`; the cells
# below state what one invocation shows: the ref each form leaves, the checksum
# each prints, and the refusal.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

family: M10
subcommand: commit
cell: commit/no-branch-refused
setup: repo tree
run: commit --repo=$REPO -s x $TREE
expect-exit: 1
expect-stdout: empty
expect-stderr: equals "error: A branch must be specified with --branch, or use --orphan"
ref-expect-exit: 1
ref-expect-stdout: empty
ref-expect-stderr: equals "error: A branch must be specified with --branch, or use --orphan"
oracle: exit-status stdout-text stderr-text refs-bytes inventory
outcome: refused-both
severity: interop
spec: format-reference.md#commit
note: a commit either names the branch it moves or states with `--orphan` that it
 writes no ref. Both refuse the pair's absence in the same words, and neither
 publishes an object, which `refs-bytes` and `inventory` state as an empty `refs/`
 and an empty object store on both sides. `commit/no-branch-fault-order` below
 cites the order the check holds.

family: M10
subcommand: commit
cell: commit/no-branch-fault-order
setup: repo tree
outcome: refused-both
severity: interop
evidence: ostrya_cli::cli::commit_parenting_matches_the_tool
spec: format-reference.md#commit
note: the missing branch is reported ahead of `--parent` and ahead of the tree, so
 the same line answers a commit that also carries an unresolvable `--parent` and
 one whose tree path does not open. Each is its own invocation, so the three
 stand together in the cited test rather than in one `run:` line.

